This rule applies when Quality OS files are in context. It does **not** replace `.cursor/rules/sai-coordination.mdc`, `.ai/` ICM work, or `openclaw-dashboard/` prototype scaffold.

Before creating or editing product architecture, read `.sai-quality/FEATURES_LOCKED` and `.sai-quality/architecture/registry.json`.

If `.sai-quality/FEATURES_LOCKED` exists, do not create product implementation under `apps/`, `services/`, `packages/`, `evals/`, or `infrastructure/`. Executable quality work stops at G03 until co-founders approve G04+ tool pinning.

Search before create. Extend canonical owners. Do not create `v2/new/legacy/tmp/copy` parallel paths.

Run `python3 scripts/qualityctl.py status` before material Quality OS work. Do not run `qualityctl unlock` or install SonarQube/Dependency-Track/Renovate without explicit co-founder approval.

Never weaken a gate, add a broad ignore, refresh a baseline, or delete a regression test merely to achieve green CI.
